{
  "schema_version": 5,
  "type": "bugfix",
  "problem": [
    {
      "text": "The tensor diagnostic's existing exclusion predicate did not cover paths containing global_vars[, local_vars[ or updated_globals[. The patch adds those three spellings.",
      "basis": "source",
      "evidence": ["call_7174c6a3ee854dfd8ebc55bd10153125"]
    }
  ],
  "reasoning": [
    {
      "text": "Filtering inside collect suppresses matching tensor references before result recording, without changing traversal or freeing tensors.",
      "basis": "source",
      "evidence": ["call_4b1d64273f3941629709f0e60f946fe3", "call_7174c6a3ee854dfd8ebc55bd10153125"]
    }
  ],
  "impact": [
    {
      "text": "The whole-parent-tree literal search found an import in quantize.py but no invocation of list_gpu_tensors. The demonstrated scope is diagnostic reporting, not a newly activated conversion path.",
      "basis": "source",
      "evidence": ["call_d35b4f6d848e4f8a80e2e52b38037a3a", "call_7174c6a3ee854dfd8ebc55bd10153125"]
    }
  ],
  "source_notes": [
    {
      "text": "The earlier debugger-filter entry describes adding dbg.value_resolve_thread_list; this patch retains that exclusion.",
      "basis": "ancestor",
      "evidence": ["call_434851e47aed452d9d75d3e5a7e1640b"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Issue #7, “quantizing model: undefined symbol: __cxa_call_terminate”, reports a native-extension import failure, not debugger-reference filtering.",
      "basis": "source",
      "evidence": ["call_d1bf41d1923d4f91a74cd92776ef04fe"]
    }
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "No live debugger session, tensor traversal or CUDA behavior was tested; the computation tested only a transcribed string predicate.",
    "Literal searches do not exclude dynamic or external callers. The provenance of the three new path spellings in debugger internals remains unverified."
  ],
  "links": ["083729ba09c51485813e707672966e12ca54b9df"],
  "chapters": [
    {
      "id": "runtime",
      "title": "Suppress additional debugger-style tensor-reference paths",
      "claims": [
        {
          "text": "list_gpu_tensors traverses globals, thread frames, attributes, dictionaries and sequences. collect applies tensor/device and size checks, then path exclusions, before grouping references by tensor identity for size-sorted, per-device tables. The patch changes only the exclusion list.",
          "basis": "source",
          "evidence": ["call_4b1d64273f3941629709f0e60f946fe3", "call_7174c6a3ee854dfd8ebc55bd10153125"]
        },
        {
          "text": "The added strings match indexed paths produced by dictionary and sequence traversal. Matching is substring-based, not debugger-object detection: ordinary application paths containing those strings are also suppressed, while another unfiltered reference can still expose the same tensor.",
          "basis": "source",
          "evidence": ["call_4b1d64273f3941629709f0e60f946fe3", "call_7174c6a3ee854dfd8ebc55bd10153125"]
        },
        {
          "text": "A standard-library predicate transcription newly excluded examples for all three added strings, retained model.weight and model.global_vars_weight, and preserved the existing debugger-thread exclusion. It also excluded model.global_vars['weight'], illustrating the name-based boundary.",
          "basis": "execution",
          "evidence": ["call_7d1e81f30868427a9398e70b779e166b"]
        },
        {
          "text": "This favors a small diagnostic-output filter over debugger-aware traversal pruning; it does not establish reduced traversal cost or memory use.",
          "basis": "inference",
          "evidence": ["call_4b1d64273f3941629709f0e60f946fe3", "call_7174c6a3ee854dfd8ebc55bd10153125"]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "findings": [],
  "summary": "Extends tensor-diagnostic path filtering with three debugger-style indexed-variable names, leaving traversal and tensor lifetime unchanged."
}
